    <briefdescription>
<para>Callback output — the DcsBios::IntegerBuffer equivalent, for outputs no built-in class covers (a custom display, an LCD, a bespoke actuator). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Calls a user-supplied callback with the decoded value whenever it changes. No <ref refid="classPinRef" kindref="compound">PinRef</ref>: the callback owns whatever hardware is involved.</para>
<para>Matching, (value &amp; mask) &gt;&gt; shift decoding and change dedup come from the <ref refid="classOpenSkyhawk_1_1AnalogOutput" kindref="compound">AnalogOutput</ref> base, so the callback runs once per change rather than once per CTRL_BCAST. It runs in <ref refid="namespacePanelGroup_1ab31c183f1fe58194e9c6e512fd9a0371" kindref="member">PanelGroup::loop()</ref> context — never from an ISR — and must not block: a slow callback delays every other output and the next CAN drain. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
